  "worked_solution": "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n2x=\\frac{7\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{11\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{7\\pi }{12}+n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{11\\pi }{12}+n\\pi \\,\\,\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=\\frac{7\\pi }{12}.$",
